"""Intel Level Zero (B60 / Xe2) HAL device-execution test suite.

These are the portable *purpose* tests from the NVIDIA/AMD HAL suites, re-expressed
for the Intel Level Zero backend and validated on the Intel Arc Pro B60. Each is
self-contained (deps = the HAL `max` + `std`, minimal-HAL style) and compiles the
kernels for `intel:xe2`.

Device selection
----------------
`ZE_AFFINITY_MASK` is left unset (see `hal_test.bzl`): the suite runs on whatever
device(s) the driver reports. On a single-B60 box that is the natural default; on a
multi-GPU box set `ZE_AFFINITY_MASK` via `--test_env=ZE_AFFINITY_MASK=<mask>` to pin
one device.

Local-memory / `.SHARED` + barrier (modular/modular#7601)
---------------------------------------------------------
Work-group tests that stage data in TRUE local (shared) memory
(`unsafe_stack_allocation[...address_space=.SHARED]`) and cross a work-group
`barrier()` are KNOWN-FLAKY on this driver/IGC build: under load they can read back
zeroed staged values. The root cause is below IGC fence emission (IGC does emit the
correct SLM + global fences + work-group barrier), i.e. in the driver's execution of
those fences / HW SLM coherency on Battlemage. See the #7601 investigation (the
`docs/investigation-7601-*` write-ups and the issue's comment trail). This PR does
NOT ship local-memory work-group tests, so the suite is safe to run concurrently; the
flakiness is documented here so it is not mistaken for a test-runner artifact.
"""

load("//max/driver/src/max_license/test:hal_test.bzl", "hal_gpu_test")

# --- Bucket A: portable primitives -------------------------------------------

# Scalar by-value kernel args + host<->device mapping.
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_add_constant")

# Portable vectorized load/store (width=4). The strided-gather part is held on
# modular/modular#7620 (G_STEP_VECTOR not legalizable by the SPIR-V/IGC backend).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_buffer_io")

# Portable FastDiv value correctness.
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_fast_div")

# --- Bucket A: index / identity primitives ----------------------------------

# thread_idx / block_idx primitives + buffer/queue APIs.
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_id")

# lane_id() primitive.
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_laneid")

# Dim (launch-config) string formatting (host-only, no kernel).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_dim")

# SIMD-width introspection (host-only, no kernel).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_targetinfo")
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_spirv_codegen")

# --- Bucket A: collectives (warp / block) -----------------------------------

# block-level barrier() op (on a global buffer; NOT the local-memory pattern above).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_barrier")

# warp.sum + block.sum (block reduction with broadcast).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_sum")

# warp.prefix_sum + block.prefix_sum (inclusive/exclusive scans).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_prefix_sum")

# Comprehensive warp-shuffle stress (shuffle_idx/up/down/xor, reduce, lane_group).
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_shuffle")

# --- Bucket A: SIMD vector ops ----------------------------------------------

# SIMD.insert[] with width-8 SIMD vectors.
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_simd_insert")

# SIMD width-4 loads + in-lane reduce_add().
hal_gpu_test("hal_test_simd_reduction")
